			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7df3a412-c789-472b-a798-121616a7fec2")
	)
	(text "USB-C is a plain 5 V sink: R95/R96 5.1k Rd on CC1/CC2, no PD. D+/D- go to the BQ25798 for BC1.2 detection.\nBC1.2 input limits (datasheet Table 7-4): SDP 0.5 A, CDP 1.5 A, DCP 3.25 A, unknown 3 A, non-standard 1-2.4 A.\nThe ILIM_HIZ pin clamps every result. HVDCP, 9 V and 12 V requests are off at power-on, so VBUS stays at 5 V.\nD1 SMBJ20A clamps VBUS. SBU is unused."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 243.84 162.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5cd1866c-cfb6-4604-90cd-c054b9ad3410")
	)
	(text "CHARGE SAFETY WITHOUT FIRMWARE (BQ25798 SLUSDV2C, checked 2026-10-19)\nPROG: R31 + R78 (2 x 6.8k = 13.6k) select 3S (12.6 V) at 750 kHz. /CE to PACK-: always charging.\nPower-on defaults: ICHG 1 A, precharge 120 mA, termination 200 mA, 12 h safety timer, JEITA, ADC off.\nILIM_HIZ: V = 1 V + 0.8 Ohm x ILIM. R32 39k / R33 24k from REGN (4.8 V typ) = 1.83 V -> ILIM 1.04 A\n(0.94-1.13 A over REGN 4.6-5.0 V). Charge at 90 % efficiency: 0.44 A at 3.5 V/cell (1C), 0.38 A at 4.1 V/cell.\nICHG stays at its 1 A default with no host, so this divider is the only rate limit.\nTS: R34 5.23k / R35 30.1k with R79 10k (no NTC): 58.9 % of REGN, inside the 10-45 C band (68.4 / 44.8 %), so\nthe charger always sees 25 C and charges at the full rate. Temperature is left to the protector (TH1).\nI2C unused: SCL/SDA pulled to REGN by R97/R98 10k (datasheet: 10k to the logic rail). /INT and /QON open.\nSTAT drives LED1 (0805 top view, lit while charging; blinks on a fault).\nCharger BAT sits on PACK+ after F1; SYS only has its caps."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 243.84 147.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9d02e1dd-0804-4f2a-9c8e-9be16f0cfd6e")
	)
	(text "BQ7791501 standalone 3S: OV 4.25 V, UV 2.8 V; R66 2 mOhm shunt -> OCD1 17.5 A (14 A worst case), OCD2 30 A, SCD 60 A, OCC 10 A.\nCCFG, CTRC, CTRD, CBI to VSS (3 cells, no stack, balancing on); PRES high via R75 (no HIBERNATE); R76 100k = EEPROM OCD delays.\nPath: cell - (BAT_N, J3 pin 1) -> R66 -> Q2 (DSG) -> Q3 (CHG) -> PACK- (J2 pin 1). F1 15 A: CELL+ -> PACK+ (J2 pin 2).\nTH1 (0603 by the FETs) is the protector's TS. Balance lead J11: pin 1 cell 1-, pin 4 cell 3+.\nOCD1/OCD2/SCD clear only on load removal: LD (R74 470k vs 200k inside) must fall under 1.25 V.\nR94 100k PACK- to BAT_N gives the charger's 17 uA (24 max) a path: PACK- about 1.5 V, LD about 0.44 V (0.62 V max).\nSo a trip clears when the pack is unplugged or the brain's switch goes off. Loads under about 48 uA count as removed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 284.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e68af004-02e8-4cdf-ba6c-bdc151a6a9e6")
	)
	(text "J3: pads for a 16 AWG pigtail with an XT30U-M; the cells' own XT30U-F plugs into it (cell leads stay uncut).\nJ2: pads for a 16 AWG lead with an XT30U-F that mates the brain's J3.\nHand-placed (DNP for PCBA): L2, Q2, Q3, R66, TH1, F1; hand-soldered: J2, J3, J11."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
